From: Marco Vitale <mrcvtl@chromium.org>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 11:02:40 +0000
Subject: [M156] [compiler] Mark JSGetTemplateObject as able to write

Original change's description:
> [compiler] Mark JSGetTemplateObject as able to write
>
> JSGetTemplateObject was marked as Operator::kEliminatable (which
> includes kNoWrite), allowing LoadElimination to keep known maps across
> it and eliminate subsequent CheckMaps nodes. However, the first
> evaluation of a tagged template literal in a realm freezes the template
> array, which copies its map and calls JSObject::OptimizeAsPrototype on
> Array.prototype, migrating a dictionary-mode Array.prototype back to
> fast properties.
>
> Remove Operator::kNoWrite from JSGetTemplateObject (using
> Operator::kNoDeopt | Operator::kNoThrow instead) and keep its control
> input when lowering to Builtin::kGetTemplateObject in JSGenericLowering.
>
> Fixed: 574339635
